[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=1236317)[0m 2. **Perturb(C)**:  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=1236317)[0m    - C is perturbed (set to 0).  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=1236317)[0m    - C is the source of D (C->D), so D is a downstream descendant of C.  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=1236317)[0m    - B is not a descendant of C, so B remains unaffected.  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=1236317)[0m    - The observation is: A:1, B:0, C:0, D:1.  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=1236317)[0m    - This aligns with the graph, as C is a descendant of A and D is a descendant of C.
